\f0\b \cf0 Encryption
\f1\b0 :\
ZIVVER generates random public and private keys.\
ZIVVER has the public and private keys of all users. But the private key is encrypted (AES symmetrical encryption) with a passkey, which is generated from the user password.\
Data from A is encrypted with the public key of B. B can then read it with his private key.\
The passkey is then asymmetrically encrypted with the public key of the receiver B. Then the passkey is thrown away and only the encrypted passkey is stored on the server.\
All recipients passkeys are encrypted.\
The organization public key is also used in the encryption of the private keys of all organization users so they can access everything. But all accesses are logged. Also useful to retrieve the users private keys in case they forget their password.\
Guest users get sent the generate passkey which is stored in a token.\
Complication: outlook can only send one token per email, even to several guest users (improvement with several emails foreseen).\
The access token contains is generated from a new encryption of the private key decrypted from the sent passkey.\
The shared token is used for unregistered users.\
The second factor is a separate logic that does not involve encryption.\
\

